Announcing net.wanted.sources!_________________________________________________

	The last article I sent to this newsgroup was a request for some
sources, followed by a trivial VMS command procedure meant to extinguish
flames sent my way (for sending a request to net.sources, that is).  This
was me cheating, in much the same way that net.jokers throw in a joke when
they're done discussing a previous joke (which they're not supposed to do).
	Anyways, this was viewed by some as arrogance; by others, with
curiosity.  A few flames *were* thrown my way, and among them came a piece
of news:

	    >>> THERE EXISTS A net.wanted.sources NEWSGROUP!!! <<<

I was pleased to hear about it, though I wonder why I hadn't heard about it
before.  I assume it's because it wasn't announced in this newsgroup.  (If
it was, I missed it.)  So as a public service, I'm announcing it here:

	    >>> THERE EXISTS A net.wanted.sources NEWSGROUP!!! <<<

	Now I can get back to work.
		<_Jym_>

P.S.:  Don't send flames.  I know this was probably already announced in
net.news.groups, but I think it will do some good here.  If you can't see
that, you're probably short-sighted enough to have voted for Reagan.

